    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "ai",
      "title": "OpenAI Agents API",
      "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/overview",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49649213",
      "score": 272,
      "comments": 150,
      "author": "aquir",
      "published": "2026-09-10T19:43:22Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Provides native primitives for multi-turn agentic workflows, automated function calling, and structured handoffs between specialized sub-agents.",
        "Evolves beyond the Assistants API by offering deeper developer control over state management, execution loops, and context persistence.",
        "Directly competes with third-party orchestration frameworks like LangChain, AutoGen, and CrewAI for building multi-agent AI architectures."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "Why Function Arguments Are Not Function Colors",
      "url": "https://jerf.org/iri/post/2026/func_args_are_not_colors/",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/tsfs3w",
      "score": 21,
      "comments": 14,
      "author": "abhin4v",
      "published": "2026-09-09T04:13:05Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Function coloring (e.g., async/await) fractures execution stacks and composability, whereas explicit arguments like contexts or allocators only alter signatures.",
        "Threading parameters like Go's context.Context or Zig allocators preserves synchronous execution semantics without requiring split runtime dispatch mechanisms.",
        "Unlike colored functions, argument-passing avoids infectious viral propagation through higher-order wrappers and standard interface abstractions."
      ]
    },
    {
